course: dictionary
lesson: 6274
title: A monk
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A monk is a man who has given his life to God and lives in a religious community called a monastery. Context tells you a lot here. «Irish monks made beautiful books such as the Book of Kells» means monks made books, so they must have been skilled writers or copiers.
explain: «Meanwhile, monks in the West copied old books by hand and kept learning alive.» Copying books by hand takes great patience, and keeping learning alive means old knowledge was saved. Monks did this in their monasteries, following rules of prayer, work and simple living.
explain: Buddhist monks live a similar life of prayer, study and meditation, but in a different religion. «A Buddhist monk» is a monk in Buddhism, and Buddhist monks often wear saffron or maroon robes. Check the clues around the word, then use a dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: A monk is a man who has given his life to God and lives in a monastery.
fact: Monks follow rules of prayer, work and simple living.
fact: In history, monks copied books by hand, made medicine and ran schools.
fact: «Irish monks made beautiful books such as the Book of Kells.»
fact: Buddhist monks live a life of prayer, study and meditation, and often wear saffron or maroon robes.
exercise: «Irish monks made beautiful books such as the Book of Kells.» Who made the books? | Kings | Traders | Vikings | *Monks
exercise: «The monk Xuanzang walked all the way to India for holy books.» Where did Xuanzang walk to? | *India | Rome | Ireland | Cambodia
exercise: «Meanwhile, monks in the West copied old books by hand and kept learning alive.» What did the monks do with the old books? | *Copied them by hand to keep learning alive | Burned them for warmth | Sold them to kings
test: What is a monastery? | *A religious community where monks live | A shop that sells silk | A large castle with a moat
test: Which rules do monks follow? | Owning lots of gold | *Prayer, work and simple living | Travelling with no rules | Hunting and feasting
exam: What colour robes do Buddhist monks often wear? | *Saffron or maroon | Black and white | Silver | Blue or green
